    <main id="main-content">
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="shell hero-grid">
          <div class="hero-copy">
            <p class="eyebrow">Open-source Visual FoxPro 9 decompiler</p>
            <h1>Get your FoxPro source back.</h1>
            <p class="lead">
              FoxLift reads compiled <code>.exe</code>, <code>.app</code>, <code>.fxp</code>, <code>.scx</code> and <code>.vcx</code> files
              and writes VFP source you can read, version and rebuild. It runs offline and never needs Visual
              FoxPro installed.
            </p>
            <div class="install">
              <code><span class="prompt">$</span> pipx install foxlift</code>
              <button type="button" data-copy="pipx install foxlift" aria-label="Copy install command">Copy</button>
            </div>
            <p class="install-alt">
              or <code>uv tool install foxlift</code> · <code>pip install foxlift</code> · Python 3.10+
            </p>
          </div>

          <figure class="terminal" aria-label="A FoxLift decompile session">
            <div class="terminal-bar" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
<pre><code><span class="prompt">$</span> foxlift decompile saveorder.fxp -o recovered/
<span class="out">&#123;
  "outdir": "recovered",
  "modules": 1,
  <span class="ok">"verified": true</span>
&#125;</span>
<span class="prompt">$</span> ls recovered/module_000000
<span class="out">meta.json  source.prg  symbols.txt</span>
<span class="prompt">$</span> cat recovered/module_000000/source.prg
<span class="k">LPARAMETERS</span> TCORDERNO
<span class="k">LOCAL</span> LNTOTAL
LNTOTAL = <span class="n">0</span>
<span class="k">SELECT</span> ORDERS
<span class="k">LOCATE FOR</span> ORDER_NO = TCORDERNO
<span class="k">IF</span> FOUND()
    LNTOTAL = ORDERS.QTY * ORDERS.PRICE
    <span class="k">REPLACE</span> ORDERS.TOTAL <span class="k">WITH</span> LNTOTAL
    MESSAGEBOX(<span class="s">"Order "</span> + TCORDERNO + <span class="s">" saved"</span>, <span class="n">64</span>, <span class="s">"Orders"</span>)
<span class="k">ELSE</span>
    <span class="k">WAIT WINDOW</span> <span class="s">"Order not found"</span> <span class="k">NOWAIT</span>
<span class="k">ENDIF</span>
<span class="k">RETURN</span> LNTOTAL</code></pre>
            <figcaption>Recompiled on VFP9, this source gives back the original bytecode and symbol table.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" id="usage">
        <div class="shell">
          <h2>Three commands.</h2>
          <div class="commands">
            <article>
              <h3>inspect</h3>
              <p>See what a binary holds — format, modules, statements, symbols — without writing anything.</p>
              <pre><code>foxlift inspect app.exe</code></pre>
            </article>
            <article>
              <h3>decompile</h3>
              <p>Lift every module to source: one directory per module with <code>source.prg</code>, <code>symbols.txt</code> and per-section verdicts in <code>meta.json</code>.</p>
              <pre><code>foxlift decompile app.exe -o recovered/</code></pre>
            </article>
            <article>
              <h3>extract</h3>
              <p>Unpack an <code>.exe</code> or <code>.app</code> into a project tree named from its own directory: <code>.prg</code> and <code>.mpr</code> source, forms and classes with their methods restored, tables and resources byte-for-byte.</p>
              <pre><code>foxlift extract app.exe -o project/</code></pre>
            </article>
          </div>

          <dl class="exit-codes">
            <div><dt>0</dt><dd>verified — every section lifted</dd></div>
            <div><dt>2</dt><dd>partial — output written, each miss marked in place with its reason</dd></div>
            <div><dt>1</dt><dd>refused — not a supported VFP file</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="hint">Add <code>--json</code> to any command for machine-readable output.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" id="figures">
        <div class="shell">
          <h2>Measured, not guessed.</h2>
          <dl class="figures">
            <div><dt>103,363<small> / 103,363</small></dt><dd>sections lift across 19 public VFP repositories</dd></div>
            <div><dt>5,476<small> / 5,476</small></dt><dd>compiled programs lift in the same repositories</dd></div>
            <div><dt>29,595<small> / 29,597</small></dt><dd>form and class sections recompile on VFP9 to the original statement bytecode</dd></div>
            <div><dt>13,976<small> / 13,978</small></dt><dd>sections lift on sealed repositories no rule was ever tuned on</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="hint">
            Every figure is checked against a real Visual FoxPro 9 SP2 compiler. <a href="https://github.com/foxlift/foxlift/tree/main/demo">Reproduce the round trip yourself.</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" id="limits">
        <div class="shell limits">
          <h2>What can't come back.</h2>
          <p>Compilation throws some things away. FoxLift proves each loss on a real VFP9 instead of inventing a replacement.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Comments</strong> are never compiled.</li>
            <li><strong>Identifier case</strong> is not kept in the symbol table.</li>
            <li><strong>DECLARE parameter names</strong> are discarded.</li>
            <li><strong>WAIT WINDOW clause order</strong> is canonicalised by the compiler.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="hint">Protected or encrypted applications are not supported. Only decompile software you own or are authorized to inspect.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
